   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "From the aperitivo to clearing the table",
     "texto": [
      "Today we talk about bars, flavours and the table.\n\n- **Before lunch:** the **aperitivo**, around one o'clock. **Ir de tapas** is to go from bar to bar.\n- **At night:** **tomar una copa** is to have a drink with someone; **ir de copas** is to go out for drinks. The next day there is sometimes a **resaca** (hangover).\n- **After a heavy meal:** an **infusión**, for example a **manzanilla**.\n- **Flavours:** **dulce**, **salado**, **amargo**, **picante** and **soso** (it lacks salt). **Casero** food is made at home: **gazpacho**, **croquetas**.\n- **Sentar:** a meal **sienta** you well or badly.\n- **The table:** **poner la mesa** (the **mantel**, the **servilletas**, a **jarra** of water) and then **recoger la mesa**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Ser, estar and sentar with food",
     "texto": [
      "To talk about flavours there are two verbs:\n\n- **Ser** says what the food is like in general: la salsa **es** picante, el café **es** amargo.\n- **Estar** says how that dish is right now: la sopa **está** sosa, hoy el café **está** muy amargo.\n\nAnd with **sentar** we say how a meal agrees with us. It works like **gustar**: the person goes with **me, te, le…** and the food is the subject.\n\n- **me sienta** well / badly · **te sienta** · **le sienta** · **nos sienta** · **os sienta** · **les sienta**\n- If the food is plural: **me sientan** mal las croquetas."
     ],
